/// Generate DSA parameters with p_len = 128, using the same bounded FIPS 186-4 parameter-generation algorithm and random-tape policy as vg_dsa_generate_parameters. Returns 1 with p||q||g, or 0 with zero output if no parameters are produced. All three tapes may affect timing. Contract: VG.Spec.Dsa.GenerationSized.contract.
///
/// # Safety
///
/// * `out` must be valid for reads and writes of `out_len` bytes.
/// * `seeds` must be valid for reads of `seeds_len` bytes.
/// * `hs` must be valid for reads of `hs_len` bytes.
/// * `witnesses` must be valid for reads of `witnesses_len` bytes.
/// * `scratch` must be valid for reads and writes of `8 * scratch_len` bytes.
/// * p_len must be 128; the (p_len, q_len) pair must be (128,20), (256,32), or (384,32).
/// * out_len must be 2*p_len + q_len; seeds_len must be a multiple of q_len; hs_len a multiple of p_len.
/// * scratch_len must be at least 64*p_len + 1024 words; destroy scratch after use.
/// * All tapes must contain fresh independent random bytes when parameter generation requires randomness.
/// * `out` and `scratch` must not overlap each other, `seeds`, `hs`, `witnesses` or the arguments on the stack (distinct Rust objects never do).
/// * None of `out`, `seeds`, `hs`, `witnesses` and `scratch` may overlap the return address on the stack or the 472 bytes of stack below it, or wrap around the end of the address space (no Rust object does).
/// * The CPU must support the `sha`, `ssse3`, `bmi2` and `adx` target features.
